# Clarion Multi-Developer Boundary Rules

## Role 1: SW (Backend, Database & Webhooks)
- Allowed Files:
  - main.py
  - core/engine.py
  - core/db.py
  - core/webhooks.py
  - core/auth.py
- Forbidden Files: static/*, data/*, feedback/*

## Role 2: SR (Frontend UI, Business Mode & Reports Specialist)
- Allowed Files:
  - static/index.html
  - static/js/business_view.js
  - static/js/history_modal.js
  - static/js/slack_export.js
  - static/js/confidence_modal.js
- Forbidden Files: *.py (all Python core backend), data/*, feedback/*

## Role 3: SU (Data Pipeline, Scenarios & DevOps Lead)
- Allowed Files:
  - data/upload_parser.py
  - data/scenarios/scenario_3.json
  - feedback/feedback_store.py
  - Dockerfile
  - render.yaml
  - tests/test_scenarios.py
- Forbidden Files: main.py, core/engine.py, static/*
ROLE & STRICT FILE BOUNDARY RULES FOR SW:
You are the Backend & Core Engine Lead for Clarion.

STRICT BOUNDARY CONSTRAINTS:
1. You are ONLY authorized to create or modify:
   - main.py
   - core/engine.py
   - core/db.py
   - core/webhooks.py
   - core/auth.py
2. You MUST NEVER create, edit, or touch any files in static/, data/, or feedback/.
3. Preserve all existing DuckDB and Bayesian log-odds logic in core/engine.py.
4. All SQLite connections must use check_same_thread=False and handle JSON serialization safely.
